    {
      "id": "claim_533dffb43e484223bf3e0e1da9e0cb93",
      "statement": "Trajectory window offsets are clamped inside the query frame's own clip rather than wrapped or dropped, so a window near a clip edge repeats its last real sample — the same thing a character standing still would produce — which keeps every frame usable instead of discarding the ends of every clip.",
